# Location-Based Attendance + Firebase App Distribution

This project is a Flutter + Firebase restaurant attendance app. Employees check in via manual tap or face+QR poster. The server (`recordAttendance` Cloud Function) is the single gatekeeper: clients send evidence, never conclusions.

**Goal 1:** Add GPS geofencing — the phone must be inside a configurable radius of the restaurant before a check-in is accepted. The server validates coordinates (uploaded as evidence), not the phone.

**Goal 2:** Document the Firebase App Distribution workflow so the APK can be uploaded and testers can install it with the Firebase App Tester app.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **GPS coordinates still come from the phone.** Advanced kernel-level spoofing is explicitly out of scope per your request. The design is as hardened as possible without moving GPS validation off-device (e.g. Play Integrity integration):
> - The **server** receives raw coordinates and decides pass/fail — the phone sends no "I am close enough" boolean
> - `isMockLocationProvider` flag from `geolocator` is **checked and rejected** server-side
> - Coordinates must arrive **fresh** (within the same 3-minute window as the photo) using the Storage upload timestamp, not the phone clock
> - Rate limiting and the presence state machine are unchanged
> - A determined attacker with root and a custom kernel can still spoof GPS — that risk is documented and out of scope

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Location fence is ON by default.** `requireLocation: true` is the default in `DEFAULT_SETTINGS`. Every new restaurant requires GPS unless an owner explicitly turns it off in the portal.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Portal location settings UI IS included.** A new "Location" card is added to the owner Settings page, allowing the owner to set lat/lng (via their browser's Geolocation or a manual input), radius, and toggle the requirement on/off.

