## Proposed Changes

### Cloud Functions

#### [MODIFY] [config.ts](file:///c:/Users/PC/Downloads/restuarant_attendence/firebase/functions/src/config.ts)
- Add `requireLocation: true`, `locationRadiusMeters: 100` to `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` (ON by default)
- Add `LOCATION_MAX_AGE_MS = PHOTO_MAX_AGE_MS` (re-use existing 3-min constant)

#### [NEW] `firebase/functions/src/lib/location.ts`
- Pure function `assertLocation(coords, restaurantSettings, now)` 
  - Validates shape (lat −90..90, lng −180..180, accuracy ≤ 150 m)
  - Rejects if `isMockLocation === true` with `LOCATION_MOCK` (also triggers audit write — see below)
  - Haversine distance check against restaurant lat/lng
  - Rejects if `timestampMs` is older than `LOCATION_MAX_AGE_MS`
  - Returns nothing on success, throws a typed error on failure

#### [MODIFY] [recordAttendance.ts](file:///c:/Users/PC/Downloads/restuarant_attendence/firebase/functions/src/callables/recordAttendance.ts)
- Extend `Base` Zod schema to accept optional `gpsCoords: { lat, lng, accuracy, isMockLocation, timestampMs }`
- After step 2 (method check), add **step 2b: location gate**
  - If `restaurant.settings.requireLocation` is true and no `gpsCoords` → reject `LOCATION_REQUIRED`
  - If coords are present → validate with `assertLocation()`
  - Rejection codes: `LOCATION_REQUIRED`, `LOCATION_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `LOCATION_MOCK`, `LOCATION_ACCURACY_LOW`, `LOCATION_STALE`
- Store `gps: { lat, lng, accuracy, distance, isMock }` on the **every** `AttendanceDoc` when coords are present — this means mock-location attempts are retained as an audit trail regardless of the rejection, visible to staff in the portal

#### [MODIFY] `firebase/functions/src/lib/errors.ts`
- Add new `REASON` constants: `LOCATION_REQUIRED`, `LOCATION_OUT_OF_RANGE`, `LOCATION_MOCK`, `LOCATION_ACCURACY_LOW`, `LOCATION_STALE`

#### [MODIFY] `firebase/functions/src/lib/types.ts`
- Add `gps?: { lat: number; lng: number; accuracy: number; distance: number }` to `AttendanceDoc`
- Add `location?: { lat: number; lng: number; radiusMeters: number }` and `requireLocation: boolean` to restaurant settings type

